#@debug@
# The packager deletes this block, contents and all, from a released build. What it holds is one
# generated line naming the checkout the game is loading, which the window title and the login
# message show in place of a version -- a working copy has no version to show. The file is
# gitignored; `npm run stamp:install` puts in the hook that writes it. Without the hook there is
# no file, and `GetVersionLabel` in `Misc.lua` answers "dev".
#
# **Do not write this block's own opening or closing marker inside a comment here.** The filter is
# a line range, so a comment quoting the closing marker ends the range early and the file name
# below survives into the TOC every user gets. That is not hypothetical -- it happened once.
DevStamp.lua
#@end-debug@

